From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lusoris <lusoris@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:52:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] avfilter/vf_tonemap_vulkan: add dynamic peak detection

Add the peak_detect and threshold options of vf_tonemap to
tonemap_vulkan. A compute shader measures the PQ luminance of the input
frame in 16x16 tiles, as the CPU detector does, and accumulates the tile
statistics and the luminance histogram in a host-visible buffer. The
host reads them back and runs the shared percentile and smoothing code
of tonemap_peak.c, then the tone map pass uses the resulting peak.

A frame that carries the lavfi.dovi.l1_max_pq metadata is not measured;
its Dolby Vision level 1 peak is used, as in vf_tonemap.

The default output with peak_detect=0 is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: lusoris <lusoris@proton.me>
---
 doc/filters.texi                          |  16 ++
 libavfilter/Makefile                      |   2 +-
 libavfilter/vf_tonemap_vulkan.c           | 283 +++++++++++++++++++++-
 libavfilter/vulkan/Makefile               |   3 +-
 libavfilter/vulkan/tonemap_peak.comp.glsl | 149 ++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 448 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 libavfilter/vulkan/tonemap_peak.comp.glsl

diff --git a/doc/filters.texi b/doc/filters.texi
index 286c6b2992147c5c78756170b9aac79b0e3e4fe3..9706f6408b28e6a2fe841cb3747a02ccc0d9cedf 100644
--- a/doc/filters.texi
+++ b/doc/filters.texi
@@ -29643,6 +29643,22 @@ ITU-R BT.2408 tone mapping with Hable curve on IPT intensity.
 Signal peak override, in units of 100 cd/m^2 (nits / 100). Default is @code{0},
 which means the peak is determined from frame metadata.
 
+@item peak_detect
+Measure the signal peak from each frame instead of taking it from
+@option{peak} or the frame's side data. The luminance is measured in PQ over
+16x16 tiles, the frame peak is the 99.995th percentile, and the result is
+smoothed over about 20 frames, as libplacebo does. A frame that carries the
+@code{lavfi.dovi.l1_max_pq} metadata, which the @code{dovi_reshape} filter
+writes, is not measured: its Dolby Vision level 1 peak is used instead.
+Default is 0 (disabled).
+
+@item threshold
+Set the scene change window of @option{peak_detect}. A change of the
+frame's average PQ level below @code{5 * threshold} percent is smoothed, a
+change above @code{15 * threshold} percent resets the smoothing to the new
+frame, and a change in between blends the two. 0 disables scene change detection.
+Default is 0.2, a window of 1 to 3 percent.
+
 @item format
 Output software pixel format of the hardware frames. Can be @code{nv12} or
 @code{p010}. Default is @code{nv12}.
